# UI prototype first (Mosaic)

Any ticket that **changes a page's look or layout** must produce a **standalone HTML prototype** before implementation lands in `public/`.

## Where prototypes live

- Path: `docs/design/prototypes/<ms-key>-<slug>.html` (e.g. `MS-400-settings-cards.html`).
- **Never** under `public/` and never behind Hosting.

## How prototypes are built

- Link the real stylesheets by **relative path** from the prototype file:
  - **Desktop:** `../../../public/fonts.css` and `../../../public/mosaic.css`
  - **Phone:** `../../../public/mobile/tokens.css` and `../../../public/mobile-shell.css` (plus `fonts.css` when the screen needs it)
- Also link the **icon font by absolute URL** — `https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Material+Symbols+Outlined:wght,FILL@100..700,0..1&display=swap`, the query `public/fonts.css` itself cites above its vendored copy. Relative paths are not enough: `fonts.css` declares its `@font-face src` as `fonts/files/*.woff2`, which resolves against the document's own directory, and htmlpreview inlines the sheet it fetched — so the font 404s and every Material Symbols ligature renders as the literal word (`church`, `menu_book`, `warning`). Absolute URLs are for prototypes only; a page under `public/` uses the vendored copy and needs no network.
- Use real **`m-*`** component classes and design tokens; prototype-only CSS goes in an inline `<style>` block and must use `var(--token)` from the linked sheets.
- **Fictional data only** — no real congregation names, people, or records (the repo is public).
- Must read correctly at **390px** and **1280px** width.
- Show **empty**, **one**, **many**, and **error** states on the same page (labelled sections).
- When there is a real design choice, show **2–3 structurally different variants** labelled **A / B / C** (not colour-only tweaks).

## Review passes (before the draft PR)

1. **`frontend-design`** — layout, hierarchy, copy, critique pass (Mosaic override: design system is the brief).
2. **`web-interface-guidelines`** — run against the prototype file per `.cursor/skills/web-interface-guidelines/SKILL.md`.

## Draft PR workflow

1. Commit **only** the prototype (and any docs tied to it).
2. Open a **draft** PR titled `[Prototype] MS-XXX` (not the implementation PR).
3. Attach screenshots at **390×844** and **1280×800**.
4. Post the view link (primary — use the format that loads relative CSS; see below) with a **3-line summary** of what changed and what you want feedback on.
5. Open the link yourself and confirm Mosaic CSS loaded (fonts, cream background, token-driven styles) **and that icons render as glyphs, not as their ligature names** — check the rendered pixels or the icon's computed `font-family`, because the stylesheet applying does not mean the font file arrived.
6. **Stop** until Jonathan approves. Implementation PR follows in a separate branch/PR.

### View links

Use the commit SHA that contains the prototype file.

- **Primary:** `https://htmlpreview.github.io/?https://github.com/JonathanHarris15/mosaic-website/blob/<commitSHA>/docs/design/prototypes/<file>.html`
- **Backup:** `https://raw.githack.com/JonathanHarris15/mosaic-website/<commitSHA>/docs/design/prototypes/<file>.html` (click through the githack interstitial once; relative `../../../public/*.css` links resolve via raw.githack)

Both formats were verified to load `fonts.css` and `mosaic.css` and apply the cream background and Cinzel/Libre Franklin stack when the prototype uses the relative paths above.

## When to skip (state the reason in the PR)

- Pure bug fix with no layout change
- Copy-only change
- Style fix of **10 lines or fewer** with no layout change
- Jonathan explicitly says no prototype

## Smoke test

Prototype-only commits **skip** the jev smoke test. The **implementation** PR that follows still runs jev in full per `.cursor/rules/smoke-test.mdc`.

## Supersedes in-app `?variant=` prototypes

This rule supersedes the `?variant=` on-route approach in `.cursor/skills/prototype/UI.md` and related prototype docs **unless Jonathan asks for in-app variants**. Point new look/layout work here instead.
